  "id": "COMPOUND:34580 - PROTEIN:1650",
  "verbalization": "Isoswinholide B is implicated in the regulation of Tyrosine-protein kinase CSK through multiple indirect pathways. The drug is predicted to target Serine/threonine-protein kinase Nek5 and Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 13, both of which are targets of Phytolaccoside B, which in turn directly interacts with Tyrosine-protein kinase CSK. This suggests a potential downstream effect of Isoswinholide B on the kinase activity of CSK, possibly through the activation or inhibition of upstream kinases. Additionally, Isoswinholide B is predicted to interact with Hs68, which is a target of a complex compound, and this complex ultimately targets CSK. The consistent scores across the three paths indicate a robust, mechanistically plausible link between Isoswinholide B and CSK, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway involving kinase modulation, but further experimental validation is required to confirm the direct interaction and functional role of Isoswinholide B in CSK regulation.",
